! Step 19 hand-back

Head `19048159c1c5beec52f72c049e5c53dc20cb6779`; state counter stays 19; no live seats, commit, or push. Next unused relay request: 037. Requests 035–036 resolved; receipt helper has a 120-second LIVENESS bound naming a broker that may have died; no timeout occurred.

The uncommitted fleet watcher now queues an attach request received during an in-flight open, retrying once that open fails, and daemon bag changes request attachment again. Request 035 ran the focused test red: the queued wake was lost (1 failure, 3 controls green). Request 036 passed all 4 tests, including the already-attached control. `git diff --check` passes. This only provides event-driven recovery: a failed open with no subsequent daemon bag change has no guaranteed retry. The test drives the watcher directly, not actual node/browser vessel composition or the daemon subscription; prove a real causal retry source and lifecycle recovery in both vessels. The previous unused ring invalidation callback remains uncommitted and has no consumer; resolve after proving direct observation or wire it safely.

Critical outstanding: `absorbCapEvents` can mutate Keyhive before its await returns. Add a guarded or serialized commit boundary and red with control exercising the authority mutation; post-await proof-version checking cannot cure it. Live browser/node proof of attachment, refold and local replica behavior remains outstanding; `onRefold` after rejection cannot certify publication. Founder lineage freshness and tri-state ring, blind-read residues and daemon join TOCTOU, independently complete dyad census (fleet board has no roster), and `runApplyAdmitPayload`, holder-session-proof and leaf-peer-proof remain owed. Preserve roll guard and epoch fields. Follow the named single-file broker test rule for daemon packages; run whole non-daemon suites before ready; e2e stays in CI. Obtain blind Opus custody read before land; no push without controller go.

<<~/ahu>>

